@PaymentApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5103

### The payment service has no login. Orders calls it directly, so the requests here go straight to port 5103.
### The order number is the idempotency key. The same number is charged once and always gets the same answer.
### The failures are settings of the service, not of a call. See the demo readme, chapter Payment service.

### PaymentRequest => OK, approved (an amount up to 500 euro)
POST {{PaymentApi_HostAddress}}/payments HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9001",
  "amount": 42.50
}

### PaymentRequest => OK, the same answer and the same reference as above, and nothing is charged again
POST {{PaymentApi_HostAddress}}/payments HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9001",
  "amount": 42.50
}

### PaymentRequest => OK, declined (an amount above 500 euro)
POST {{PaymentApi_HostAddress}}/payments HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9002",
  "amount": 500.01
}

### PaymentRequest => Bad request, no order number and no amount
POST {{PaymentApi_HostAddress}}/payments HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "",
  "amount": 0
}
